          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. Match the entries in Column I with those in Column II."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.298,
            0.107,
            0.88,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 2,
              "bbox": [
                0.298,
                0.107,
                0.88,
                0.299
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_16_table_2.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>Column I</td><td>Column II</td></tr><tr><td>(i) Concave mirror</td><td>(a) Spherical mirror with a reflecting surface that curves inwards.</td></tr><tr><td>(ii) Convex mirror</td><td>(b) It forms an image which is always erect and diminished in size.</td></tr><tr><td>(iii) Convex lens</td><td>(c) Object placed behind it may appear inverted at some distance.</td></tr><tr><td>(iv) Concave lens</td><td>(d) Object placed behind it always appears diminished in size.</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.31,
            0.882,
            0.37
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. The following question is based on Assertion/Reason. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Assertion:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Convex mirrors are preferred for observing the traffic behind us."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.295,
            0.374,
            0.882,
            0.413
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reason:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Convex mirrors provide a significantly larger view area than plane mirrors."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.296,
            0.417,
            0.557,
            0.437
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Choose the correct option:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.3,
            0.44,
            0.882,
            0.479
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation for Assertion."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.295,
            0.481,
            0.882,
            0.52
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation for Assertion."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.29,
            0.521,
            0.762,
            0.542
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.29,
            0.544,
            0.738,
            0.565
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.259,
            0.571,
            0.882,
            0.631
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11. In Fig. 10.27, note that O stands for object, M for mirror, and I for image. Which of the following statements is true?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.634,
            0.882,
            0.672
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Figure (a) indicates a plane mirror and Figure (b) indicates a concave mirror."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.296,
            0.674,
            0.882,
            0.713
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Figure (a) indicates a convex mirror and Figure (b) indicates a concave mirror."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.291,
            0.715,
            0.882,
            0.754
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "indicates a convex mirror."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
